red in the Godot global script class cache:\n\n**Path:** `/workspace/.godot/global_script_class_cache.cfg`\n```\n\"class\": &\"BattleUnit\",\n\"base\": &\"Area2D\",\n\"path\": \"res://scenes/battle_unit/battle_unit.gd\"\n```\n\n---\n\n## 7. UnitStats Class Definition\n\n**Search:** `class_name UnitStats`\n\nFound in exactly **one** file:\n\n**Path:** `/workspace/data/units/unit_stats.gd`, line 1\n\n```gdscript\nclass_name UnitStats\nextends Resource\n```\n\nAlso registered in the global script class cache:\n\n**Path:** `/workspace/.godot/global_script_class_cache.cfg`\n```\n\"class\": &\"UnitStats\",\n\"base\": &\"Resource\",\n\"path\": \"res://data/units/unit_stats.gd\"\n```\n\n---\n\n## 8. Team Enum Definition\n\n**Search:** `enum Team`, `Team.PLAYER`, `Team.ENEMY`\n\nFound in exactly **two** files:\n\n**a) Definition — `/workspace/data/units/unit_stats.gd`, line 4:**\n```gdscript\nenum Team {PLAYER, ENEMY}\n```\n\n**b) Usage reference (in the task instructions) — `/workspace/task_config.json`, line 2:**\n```\nTeam.PLAYER, Team.ENEMY\n```\n(The `task_config.json` instruction references `Team.PLAYER` and `Team.ENEMY` in the context of defining a `TARGET` dictionary and setting collision layers/masks.)\n\n**Usage in resource files** (team values as integers):\n- `bjorn.tres`: `team = 0` (which maps to `Team.PLAYER`)\n- `zombie.tres`: `team = 1` (which maps to `Team.ENEMY`)\n\n---\n\n## Summary of Key Architectural Facts\n\n| Item | Value |\n|---|---|\n| **Godot version** | 4.4 (gl_compatibility renderer) |\n| **Project name** | \"Detect Range Target Finder\" |\n| **Main scene** | `res://scenes/main.tscn` |\n| **Registered script classes** | `BattleUnit` (extends Area2D), `UnitStats` (extends Resource) |\n| **Team enum** | `Team {PLAYER=0, ENEMY=1}` defined in `UnitStats` |\n| **Player unit resource** | `bjorn.tres` — team 0 (PLAYER), attack_range 4 |\n| **Enemy unit resource** | `zombie.tres` — team 1 (ENEMY), attack_range 1 |\n| **Main scene layout** | GuardUnit (g